#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:8
msgid "What is this all about?"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:13
msgid "The Tool"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:15
msgid "The Sketch Map Tool is an easy-to-use tool for participatory mapping through offline collection,\n"
"            digitization, and georeferencing of local data. The low-tech solution is designed to simplify the collection\n"
"            and analysis of local spatial knowledge and perceptions with pens and paper maps, the so-called Sketch Maps.\n"
"            The Sketch Map Tool is an open-source web application. It facilitates the creation, usage and the\n"
"            digitization of paper-based maps with OpenStreetMap and satellite data."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:23
msgid "Sketch Map Tool Mapping"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:27
msgid "The Sketch Map Tool supports users in all the important steps of offline participatory mapping, from\n"
"            creating paper maps to digitizing them."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:31
msgid "Step 1: Create paper maps to collect data (online access needed)"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:34
msgid "Define your area of interest and your base map (<a href=\"https://wiki.osm.org\" target=\"_blank\">OpenStreetMap (OSM)</a>, <a href=\"https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=10df2279f9684e4a9f6a7f08febac2a9\"\n"
"                                target=\"_blank\">satellite imagery by ESRI </a> or <a href=\"https://openaerialmap.org/\"\n"
"                                target=\"_blank\">OpenAerialMap imagery (OAM)</a>), look at the OSM Map Quality check provided by  \n"
"            <a href=\"https://api.quality.ohsome.org/\" target=\"_blank\">HeiGIT ohsome quality API</a> and export the map as a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:41
msgid "Step 2: Participatory Mapping"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:44
msgid "Offline data collection with local communities, either individually or as a group activity. Participants mark their local knowledge directly onto printed Sketch Maps with pens."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:48
msgid "Step 3: Paper to GIS (online access needed)"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:51
msgid "Scan or photograph your marked Sketch Maps, upload the images to the Sketch Map Tool and download collected markings (geojson and geotiff).\n"
"        \tThe tool georeferences the Sketch Maps and detects the markings employing a fusion of computer vision algorithms and novel AI models. \n"
"        \tThe results can then be used for further analysis in Geographic Information System software."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:59
msgid "Video preview image for Introduction to the Sketch Map Tool"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:67
msgid "Introduction to the Sketch Map Tool"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:72
#: sketch_map_tool/templates/case-study-cultural-landmarks.html:55
#: sketch_map_tool/templates/case-study-timor-leste.html:42
msgid "The Project"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:74
msgid "The Sketch Map Tool project has been developed in close cooperation between the <a\n"
"                href=\"https://heigit.org\" target=\"_blank\">HeiGIT</a> and the <a\n"
"                href=\"https://www.geog.uni-heidelberg.de/de/institut/geoinformatik\" target=\"_blank\">GIScience Research Group</a>\n"
"            from Heidelberg University with the generous contributions of several sponsors and support by partner\n"
"            organizations."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:82
msgid "Sketch Map Tool, Timeline."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:85
msgid "From Prototype to Global Tool"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:87
msgid "The development of the Sketch Map Tool began in 2018 as an idea and simple prototype in the <a\n"
"                href=\"https://www.geog.uni-heidelberg.de/en/giscience/sketch-map-tool\" target=\"_blank\">Waterproofing\n"
"                Data project</a> (funded by the Federal Ministry of Education and Research - BMBF). In 2021, this initial prototype received a major update, \n"
"                including an improved user interface and the first implementation of color detection (using computer vision)"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:93
msgid "Since then, the tool has been tested by humanitarian organizations worldwide, including in Germany, Chile, Colombia, Brazil, Mozambique, Madagascar,\n"
"            Honduras, Ghana, Kenya, and Sudan. Following its 2023 relaunch as a stable version, the Sketch Map Tool is now an official part of the <a href=\"https://heigit.org/heigit-technology/\" target=\"_blank\">HeiGIT tool suite</a>."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:96
msgid "Milestones & Key Features"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:98
msgid "The tool is continuously evolving to meet the needs of humanitarian actors:"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:101
msgid "2024 Relaunch of the stable version: implementation of satellite imagery as a base map, a massive improvement in color detection, and the creation of customized training materials to make the tool accessible to end-users with different knowledge levels."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:102
msgid "2025 Update: Integration of OpenAerialMap (OAM) as an additional base map source and the implementation of point detection."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:103
msgid "Ongoing Improvement: Regular updates to the underlying Machine Learning models alongside general maintenance and stability improvements."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:106
msgid "Our supporters"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:110
msgid "The continuous development and adaptation of the Sketch Map Tool for humanitarian use has been made possible through a strong collaboration with the German Red Cross (GRC) \n"
"            and significant financial support from the German Federal Foreign Office within the framework of the \"Global Project II.\" This project contributes to reducing the negative consequences \n"
"            of disasters for affected populations by extending strategic humanitarian topics and innovative approaches. Core maintenance of the tool and regular updates to the machine learning models are ensured by core funding from the Klaus Tschira Foundation (KTS)."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:115
msgid "The focus of the relaunch in 2024, once again funded within the framework of the <em>Globalprojekt\n"
"                II</em>, was the implementation of satellite\n"
"            images as a base map and the overall improvement of color detection, especially on satellite images. \n"
"            Additionally, general software stability\n"
"            was further ensured, and customized training materials designed to make the tool more accessible to end-users with\n"
"            different knowledge levels."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:123
msgid "The Vision"
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:125
msgid "We envision a world in which communities worldwide are empowered to collect, communicate, and utilize local\n"
"            spatial information and knowledge\n"
"            effectively through an open-source, low-tech, participatory mapping solution. This solution bridges paper-based data\n"
"            collection with digital analysis\n"
"            and storage, aiming for collaborative visualization and analysis of current and past conditions and perceptions. The\n"
"            goal is to raise awareness and\n"
"            co-create transformative change in areas impacted by sustainability challenges."
msgstr ""

#: sketch_map_tool/templates/about.html:134
msgid "If you have questions or would like to provide feedback, please reach out to the <a\n"
"                href=\"mailto:sketch-map-tool@heigit.org\">project team</a>."
msgstr ""

